  "findings": [
    "The inserted point is exactly M+epsilon*q, and the return vector is B-M-epsilon*q. Expanding the determinant explicitly proves each area and height identity. The incoming height of B and the constant return height of A are both det(M-A,B-M), with the correct ordered signs.",
    "The attachment signs hold for every positive epsilon, including possible zero determinants. The small crossing theorem adds exactly the three nonzero local determinants: parent turn, incoming/q and q/outgoing. It does not assume an already generic inserted polygon.",
    "Continuity of the sign at two nonzero constant terms gives a common positive radius via min. The repaired singleton conversion changes no theorem statement or mathematical argument.",
    "The first and second strict-straddle tests are both retained. Their conjunction is exactly both attachment signs equal to the parent turn. The source segment-crossing criterion identifies intersection in both open segments and transversality with these tests.",
    "All four endpoint heights are independently shown nonzero. Therefore every closed-segment solution has both parameters strictly between zero and one. This excludes endpoint-only contacts in non-loop sectors, rather than conflating closed and open intersections.",
    "The final theorem also exports both direction-determinant signs on that same interval. No division by a possibly zero sign, geometric oracle, root independence or sector exclusion is introduced."
  ],
  "limits": "Local incoming/return pair only. Cyclic indexing, global inherited crossings, G2, one chamber and Gauss-word claims are not established here. Stronger fidelity and canonical integration remain pending."
